, "tokens_after": 76139, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 323, "window": [246, 30246], "direction": "both"}, "result_digest": "44f1705f99868718", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"both\", \"n_neighbors\": 30, \"neighbors\": [39, 55, 68, 118, 139, 306, 337, 425, 441, 585, 722, 788, 794, 901, 955, 977, 1008, 1009, 1057, 1145, 1147, 1181, 1247, 1387, 1444, 1702, 1725, 1734, 1840, 1847], \"node\": 323, \"window\": [246, 30246]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 76139, "tokens_after": 76139, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_8b4a3bfa", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "regime_switch", "entities": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776], "window": [246, 30246], "confidence": 0.87, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No abrupt regime switch. With the prescribed 5000 half-window, the group's contact set before and after the best candidate change point (t=13963) overlaps at Jaccard 0.74 (31 of 40/33 shared), and turnover stays flat at 0.17-0.30 all period. The group's members all contact one fixed ~30-node panel; members simply take turns (323/477 early, 1639/1776 late), so edge-level diffs show Jaccard 0 purely because the left endpoint changes while the right endpoints are identical. Sharper spikes at bandwidth 2500 are sparsity artifacts in a 9-event lull where the after-set is a strict subset of the before-set. Volume is stable with no bursts, ruling out an activity shock."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\nThe apparent turnover is an artifact of **member rotation over a fixed contact panel**, not a change of partners.\n\n**Key findings:**\n\n1. **Contact-set overlap is high across the candidate change point.** At the prescribed half-window of 5000, the peak turnover (t=13963) gives 40 before-contacts and 33 after-contacts sharing 31 \u2014 Jaccard \u2248 0.74 (step_01, step_10). Peak change of only 0.30 is nowhere near a regime switch, and the series is flat (0.17\u20130.30) across the entire period \u2014 the signature of gradual background turnover.\n\n2. **The external panel is literally identical for early and late members.** Node 323 (active only in [246,5246], 90 events) and node 1776 (active only in [25246,30246], 90 events) both contact the *same* 30-node panel {39, 55, 68, 118, 139, 306, 337, 425, 441, 585, 722, 788, 794, 901, 955, 977, 1008, 1009, 1057, 1145, 1147, 1181, 1247, 1387, 1444, 1702, 1725, 1734, 1840, 1847} (step_15, step_16; same for 1039 and 1530, step_05/step_06).\n\n3. **The Jaccard=0 in edge-level diffs is misleading.** step_07 reports jaccard 0.0 between the first and last 5000 units, but inspection of the added/removed samples shows the removed edges are (323,\u00b7),(477,\u00b7) and the added edges are (1639,\u00b7),(1776,\u00b7) over the *same* right-hand endpoints. Only *which member* is on duty changes. step_13/step_14 confirm the baton pass: 323/477/865 carry all early activity, 1639/1776 all late activity.\n\n**Confounder controls:** Volume is stable with no bursts (step_02: 41\u2013118 per bin; step_09: zero bursts at z=1.5), so no event-rate shock. The sharp-looking spikes at bandwidth 2500 (0.74 at t=13643, 0.73 at t=16207) are sparsity artifacts \u2014 step_12 shows those windows hold just 9 events vs ~95 in neighbours, and the \"after\" set at t=13643 is a strict *subset* of the \"before\" set (a truncated tail, not a new cohort). Staggered co-activity (step_08, max Jaccard 0.6) reflects overlapping shifts, not a synchronized switch.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8b4a3bfa\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [323, 477, 865, 889, 1039, 1119, 1389, 1432, 1530, 1553, 1639, 1776],\n  \"window\": [246, 30246],\n  \"confidence\": 0.87,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No abrupt regime switch. With the prescribed 5000 half-window, the group's contact set before and after the best candidate change point (t=13963) overlaps at Jaccard 0.74 (31 of 40/33 shared), and turnover stays flat at 0.17-0.30 all period. The group's members all contact one fixed ~30-node panel; members simply take turns (323/477 early, 1639/1776 late), so edge-level diffs show Jaccard 0 purely because the left endpoint changes while the right endpoints are identical. Sharper spikes at bandwidth 2500 are sparsity artifacts in a 9-event lull where the after-set is a strict subset of the before-set. Volume is stable with no bursts, ruling out an activity shock.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 90198, "total_output_tokens": 6704, "total_tokens": 96902, "total_latency_ms": 100044, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}